    "text": "To determine the total cost of all 5 shirts, we need to calculate the cost of the shirts that cost $15 each and the cost of the shirts that cost $20 each, and then sum these amounts.\n\nFirst, we calculate the cost of the 3 shirts that each cost $15:\n\\[\n3 \\times 15 = 45\n\\]\nSo, the total cost of the 3 shirts is $45.\n\nNext, we calculate the cost of the remaining 2 shirts, each of which cost $20:\n\\[\n2 \\times 20 = 40\n\\]\nSo, the total cost of the 2 shirts is $40.\n\nNow, we add the two amounts together to find the total cost of all 5 shirts:\n\\[\n45 + 40 = 85\n\\]\nTherefore, the total cost of all 5 shirts is \\(\\boxed{85}\\).",
